<title>BELGIUM: France sees 97 welfare deficit at 30 bln FFR.</title>
<headline>France sees 97 welfare deficit at 30 bln FFR.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>France expects to reduce its welfare deficit to 0.3 percent of GDP or 30 billion francs in 1997, according to a convergence plan approved by EU finance ministers on Monday.</p>
<p>The figure was contained in a detailed plan which aimed to reduce the total public deficit to 3.0 percent of gross domestic product this year.</p>
<p>Officials said the forecasts were based on figures drawn up last year and did not necessarily take account of recent trends. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
